<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n107001" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπαυγάζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>shine under, gleam beneath,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρυσοῦ ψῆγμα ποταμῷ ἀργυροδίνῃ
					ὑπαυγάζον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VS</u>
					2.1.14
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ μαζοὶ ὀρθοὶ ὑπαυγάζουσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Im.</u>
					2.8
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>begin to shine, dawn,</i> of daybreak, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>VH</u>
				2.47
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Polyaen.
				7.8.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> trans.,
				<i>light up,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀστὴρ ὁλκὸν ὑπαυγάζων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					3.1378
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Dam.
				<u>Isid.</u>
				63
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
